@startuml
title class diagram - RobotInputState node

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospace

class RobotInputState <<rclpy.node.Node>> {
  -_reference_frame: str
  -_hand_frame: str
  -_head_frame: str
  -_head_pan_joint: str
  -_head_tilt_joint: str
  -_gripper_left_joint: str
  -_gripper_right_joint: str
  -_gripper_min_position_m: float
  -_gripper_max_position_m: float
  -_head_pan_sign: float
  -_head_tilt_sign: float
  -_max_state_age_sec: float
  -_joint_positions: dict[str, float]
  -_last_joint_state_sec: float
  -_joint_lock: threading.Lock
  -_tf_buffer: tf2_ros.Buffer
  -_tf_listener: TransformListener
  -_on_joint_state(message: JointState): void
  +get_snapshot(): dict
  -_lookup_transform(source_frame, errors): TransformStamped | None
}

class JointState {
  +name: string[]
  +position: float[]
}

class Buffer {
  +lookup_transform(target_frame, source_frame, time)
}

class TransformListener

class "helper functions" as Helpers {
  +_head_command_quaternion(pan, tilt, pan_sign, tilt_sign): dict
  +_transform_pose(transform): dict
}

RobotInputState --> JointState : subscribes /joint_states
RobotInputState --> Buffer : lookup wrist/head TF
RobotInputState --> TransformListener : owns listener
RobotInputState --> Helpers : formats snapshot fields

note bottom of RobotInputState
  /robot_state returns ready=false when required
  joint states or transforms are missing or stale.
end note

@enduml
